.TH FLAMESHOT 1 "2026-11-07" "Flameshot 15.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
flameshot \- screenshot capture and annotation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B flameshot
.RI [ command ] " [ options ]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Flameshot captures screenshots, provides an annotation editor, copies or saves
images, and pins images above other windows. Running without a command starts
the background service and, when enabled, its tray icon; it does not take a screenshot.
.PP
X11 capture and Wayland desktop screenshot portals are supported. On Wayland,
portal permissions and available operations depend on the desktop environment.
A graphical session and its session D-Bus are required for capture and desktop actions.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B gui
Capture, select a region and edit annotations. On a multi-monitor desktop a monitor
chooser may appear unless a monitor or the entire desktop was explicitly selected.
.TP
.B screen
Capture one monitor. On X11 the default is the monitor containing the pointer.
On Wayland, specify a monitor with
.BR \-\-number .
.TP
.B full
Capture the entire desktop without opening the annotation editor.
.TP
.B launcher
Open the capture launcher.
.TP
.B config
Open the settings window when no configuration options are supplied; otherwise
update the requested settings or check the configuration.
.TP
.B history
Open upload history. Available only in builds with Imgur support.
.TP
.B updates
Open the update checker. Available only in builds with update checking enabled.
.TP
.B help
Show help, optionally for a command, for example
.BR "flameshot help gui" .
.SH GENERAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Show help. Each command also accepts this option.
.TP
.BR \-v , " " \-V , " " \-\-version
Show version information without starting the background service.
.SH CAPTURE OPTIONS
Capture and configuration options may be repeated. The first supplied value is used;
all occurrences of checked values must be valid. Repeating a switch keeps it enabled.
The following options apply to
.BR gui , " " screen " and " full .
.TP
.BR \-p , " " \-\-path " " \fIPATH\fR
Save to an existing directory or an image filename. Directories use the configured
filename pattern. Existing images are not overwritten; a distinct filename is chosen.
.TP
.BR \-d , " " \-\-delay " " \fIMILLISECONDS\fR
Delay capture by the given number of milliseconds, from 0 through 2147483647.
The default is zero.
.TP
.BR \-c , " " \-\-clipboard
Copy the resulting image to the clipboard. This can be combined with an output path.
.TP
.BR \-r , " " \-\-raw
Write PNG image bytes to standard output. Redirect this output to a file or pipe.
Diagnostics are written to standard error. An explicit output path still requests
saving in addition to writing PNG bytes.
.PP
With no raw output, clipboard, pin, geometry output or explicit editor action,
the result is saved using the configured output directory. Clipboard-related
configuration can also request saving a copy or copying a saved path.
.SH GUI AND SCREEN OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-region " REGION"
Select a region in capture-image pixel coordinates. A rectangle uses
.IR WIDTHxHEIGHT+X+Y ;
negative offsets can use minus signs. The value
.B all
selects the whole captured image. For
.B gui
only,
.BI screen N
selects monitor number N, starting at zero.
.TP
.B \-\-pin
Pin the captured image above other windows.
.SH GUI OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-last-region
Reuse the previous selection where it overlaps the current capture. An explicit
.B \-\-region
has priority.
.TP
.BR \-s , " " \-\-accept-on-select
Accept immediately after making a selection.
.TP
.BR \-g , " " \-\-print-geometry
Print the selection as WIDTHxHEIGHT+X+Y. When combined with
.BR \-\-raw ,
PNG output takes priority.
.SH SCREEN OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n , " " \-\-number " " \fIINDEX\fR
Select a zero-based monitor index, from 0 through 2147483647.
The selected index must identify an active monitor.
.TP
.BR \-e , " " \-\-edit
Open the editor for the selected monitor.
.SH CONFIGURATION OPTIONS
Boolean values must be explicitly supplied as
.B true
or
.BR false .
Only requested settings are changed; unrelated settings are preserved.
.TP
.BR \-a , " " \-\-autostart " " \fIBOOLEAN\fR
Enable or disable startup with the desktop session.
.TP
.BR \-f , " " \-\-filename " " \fIPATTERN\fR
Set the filename pattern. This is a pattern, not a directory path.
.TP
.BR \-n , " " \-\-notifications " " \fIBOOLEAN\fR
Enable or disable notifications.
.TP
.BR \-t , " " \-\-trayicon " " \fIBOOLEAN\fR
Enable or disable the tray icon.
.TP
.BR \-s , " " \-\-showhelp " " \fIBOOLEAN\fR
Enable or disable editor help text.
.TP
.BR \-m , " " \-\-maincolor " " \fICOLOR\fR
Set the main interface color.
.TP
.BR \-k , " " \-\-contrastcolor " " \fICOLOR\fR
Set the contrasting interface color. Quote hexadecimal colors in the shell.
Interface colors must be opaque. QColor forms #RGB, #RRGGBB, #RRRGGGBBB
and #RRRRGGGGBBBB are accepted, as are named colors.
The #AARRGGBB form requires an alpha value of FF.
These command-line colors are stored as normalized #RRGGBB values.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Validate configuration values and shortcut assignments without opening the settings window.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/flameshot/flameshot.ini
Configuration file. The usual default is
.IR ~/.config/flameshot/flameshot.ini .
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/flameshot/flameshot/region.txt
Cached capture selection. The usual cache root is
.IR ~/.cache .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful operation, help or version display.
.TP
.B 1
An operation failed, for example because of invalid configuration or a desktop service error.
.TP
.B 2
Capture was cancelled or command-line arguments were rejected.
.TP
.B 3
The session D-Bus connection could not be established, or the background service
lost its established connection.
.TP
.B 130
The background service received SIGINT.
.TP
.B 143
The background service received SIGTERM.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B flameshot gui
Select and annotate an image.
.TP
.B flameshot gui \-\-region 400x300+100+100 \-\-raw > capture.png
Edit a preset region and write the resulting PNG to a file.
.TP
.B flameshot full \-p ~/Pictures \-d 2000
Capture the desktop after two seconds and save in Pictures.
.TP
.B flameshot screen \-n 0 \-c
Copy the first monitor to the clipboard.
.TP
.B flameshot config \-\-notifications false \-\-trayicon true
Change notification and tray preferences.
.TP
.B flameshot config \-\-check
Check the configuration without opening a window.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project documentation: https://flameshot.org/
.br
Source and contributors: https://github.com/flameshot-org/flameshot
